{% extends "voc2_en.j2" %}

{% block summary %}
<p>
    <em>This implementation model is an implementation model of the <a target="_blank" href="https://belgif.github.io/thematic/models/public%20services/index_en.html">ICEG application profile public service</a>
        and follows the <a target="_blank" href="https://data.vlaanderen.be/ns/dienst">OSLO Vocabulary 'Service'</a>.
        Many things are taken from the ICEG model and are therefore only described in English. Specific extensions within this data model are described in Dutch.    </em>
</p>

<p>This implementation model is used to exchange data on public services between IPDC (version 3) and LPDC.
    It describes how to communicate to and from the local product and service catalogue (LPDC) and the inter-administrative product and service catalogue (IPDC).</p>

<h4>Want to know more?</h4>
<p>A complete overview of all available concepts and instances can be found in <a target="_blank" href="https://productencatalogus-v3.vlaanderen.be">the product catalogue</a>.
    Behind the scenes, all these services are stored in <a target="_blank" href="https://www.vlaanderen.be/digitaal-vlaanderen/onze-oplossingen/interbestuurlijke-producten-en-dienstencatalogus-ipdc">IPDC</a>.
    If you wish to integrate the information about this service into your own solutions, this is possible via the
    <a target="_blank" href="https://ipdc.vlaanderen.be/docs/swagger-ui/index.html">IPDC API.</a> Be sure to take a look at
    <a target="_blank" href="https://vlaamseoverheid.atlassian.net/wiki/external/6317081715/ZGU4MGNlODM2N2U1NDU5MGFlY2NlYzcxYmQyYWUwMTc">the connection guide</a>.</p>
{% endblock %}

